Hey Jan,

I did not apply any ubuntu patch for kernel 2.6.35 (since I do not have
one).  Also, good to know that I should not use xenomai patches together
with ubuntu patches.

Anyway, the problem occurred as well with the kernel 2.6.35 (see attached
dmesg_bad_2.6.35)
I also attached the config.

Please let me know what else I could try out. Again, I haven't managed to
disable SPARSEMEM, just fyi.

THANKS so much,
 peter


On Mon, Oct 25, 2010 at 11:15 AM, Jan Kiszka <jan.kiszka@domain.hid> wrote:

> Am 25.10.2010 20:04, Peter Pastor wrote:
> > Hey Eric,
> >
> > Thanks for your prompt response. However, I do not have the "FLAT_MEMORY"
> > option available. I can only select the sparse memory model.
> >
> > I have upgraded to 2.6.35 and so far the problem has not occured.
> However, I
> > haven't used the system much. Again, it seems that a specific event
> triggers
> > the problem.
> >
> > Also, can someone tell me whether the ubuntu kernel patch is recommended
> to
> > use with Xenomai ? If so, can someone tell me how to get the patch for my
> > particular kernel version 2.6.35 ? ( I am sorry if this is the wrong
> mailing
> > list to ask this question )
>
> Xenomai is not supported over distro-patched kernels. While some of
> their patches may be orthogonal, other may have all kinds of side
> effects together with I-pipe that no one wants to track down (not that
> those patches are inherently bad, just not tested against I-pipe).
>
> If you are missing a specific feature, either port it back carefully or
> wait for it to appear in the next upstream kernel (e.g. AppAmor is now
> in 2.6.36, and I guess we will have I-pipe for that kernel within the
> next weeks).
>
> Jan
>
>

